; ACT Demo - Finding Same Color Fruits (Working Version)
; ========================================================
;
; Prerequisites:
; Create the ACT file first:
;   ./examples/misc/make_fruit_colors_act.sh
;
; Problem: Multiple ACT queries in conjunction don't work yet!
; Solution: Two-stage approach - bring data into space first, then cross-match

; Stage 1: Fetch all colors from ACT into main space
(exec (0 fetch-colors)
  (I (ACT fruit_colors (color $fruit $c)))
  (O (+ (fruit-color $fruit $c))))

; Stage 2: Cross-match fruits in the main space
; Now we can find pairs with the same color
(exec (1 find-same-color)
  (, (fruit-color $f1 $c)
     (fruit-color $f2 $c))
  (O (+ (same-color $f1 $f2 $c))))

; Expected output:
; Stage 1 brings in 6 fruit-color facts
; Stage 2 finds all pairs:
; (same-color apple apple red)
; (same-color apple strawberry red)
; (same-color strawberry apple red)
; (same-color strawberry strawberry red)
; (same-color banana banana yellow)
; (same-color banana lemon yellow)
; (same-color lemon banana yellow)
; (same-color lemon lemon yellow)
; (same-color grape grape purple)
; (same-color orange orange orange)
